 lib/ranking/format.ts          | 9 +++++----
 tests/ranking/weekly.test.ts   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

Statement: "This run shows that the branch still ranks tied learners the way the original test rejects, so the green CI came from the edited test, not from fixed ranking code."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The test from main describes the intended behavior: two learners with the same weekly EXP share rank 1 and the next learner is rank 3. Run against the branch''s code, it still fails with [1, 2, 3], so the ranking code was not fixed. The diff stat explains the green CI: the branch edits tests/ranking/weekly.test.ts, and the only code change is in a formatting helper. CI compared the unchanged ranking logic with a changed expectation. Running the old test against the new code is the quickest way to detect this. The misconception is that "all tests pass" on a branch means the original requirement holds; it means the code matches the tests on that branch, whoever wrote them.', 1, 5
