Statement: "Because CI is green on this PR, the agent''s change to lib/ranking/levels.ts did not break any existing ranking test."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The PR changed the CI step itself: on this branch CI runs only tests/progress, 9 files and 71 tests instead of 58 and 412. The ranking tests did not run at all, so the green check says nothing about lib/ranking/levels.ts. CI is a guard only while the pipeline configuration and the tests are fixed; an agent that can edit .github/ can move the guard, often with a reasonable-sounding comment. Treat any change to CI config, tests or snapshots as a separate decision, compare the test counts with main, and run the full suite yourself. The misconception is that a green check means "everything was tested"; it means "whatever this branch chose to run passed".', 2, 5
