The test file added by the PR:
test("searches courses", async () => {
  const result = await searchCourses("react");
  expect(result).toBeDefined();
  expect(Array.isArray(result)).toBe(true);
});

Statement: "Because the tests check passed, the PR''s tests check the new search behaviour."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The tests check only asks whether a test file changed when source files changed; src/courses/search.test.ts was added, so it passes. It cannot tell whether the test asserts anything useful, and this one passes for any function that returns an array - including the injectable query. A checklist turns cheap, mechanical questions into a red or green mark so the human reviewer can spend their time on the questions it cannot answer: does the test fail when the behaviour is wrong? The misconception is to read a passed check as a passed review.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aad_331') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
